# New Zion Group Onboarding Process Overview

# Group is sold by Zion Sales team

1. These groups should come directly from Account Executives who report to Preston Guthrie, currently Cameron Morris and Hayley DeHaan

# Zion Salesperson send an email to the new client with a link to the onboarding survey:

Subject: Next Steps to Get Your Group Enrolled in Zion Plans

Hi \[Client],

We’re excited to get your group set up with Zion! To ensure a smooth and timely enrollment, please complete the steps below:

1. Complete the [New Group Onboarding Form](https://forms.office.com/r/xq9jYMYPEF)  \
   This gives us the information we need to set up your group correctly.

2. Sign Your Group Contract \
   Once completed, we’ll send your contract for review and signature.

3. Meet with Your Benefit Manager \
   You’ll review your employer portal and finalize your group setup during this meeting.

4. Add Employees & Enroll \
   Upload your employee census and complete enrollment.

If you have any questions along the way or need support with any step, I’m here to help. We’re looking forward to partnering with you!

Best regards, \[Salesperson]

# Client completes onboarding [survey](https://forms.office.com/pages/responsepage.aspx?id=QjkzK-RW_Uu_WLwPq_BDgTSmUjM-QmRLoBOJMoABrDRUNTFNWkRMQkpJTTE1U1kxNFdTRzBOOTZMSS4u\&route=shorturl)

1. Salesperson could complete this for the client while on the phone with them to help expedite process
2. This could serve as full intake and notification for Account Success and ENav team to start working the group. Replacing the current form the Zion Sales team is submitting

# Data feeds to onboarding tracker to enter the queue for ENav team to build out and Benefit Manager to reach out

1. [Zion New Group Onboarding to Enav.xlsx](https://planstinhealth-my.sharepoint.com/:x:/g/personal/canenhastings_planstin_com/IQCoeBU19oh7SoYEq6hHDAYtAdfDp1sTTHZ2b-i4RWFIY0o?e=yD6qMU)
2. This replaces the current tracker: [New Company Notifications - Zoho Sheet](https://workdrive.zohoexternal.com/sheet/open/ogztdd5634e83e04a4a93ae4b40c255206cbf?sheetid=0\&range=S10\&authId=%7B%22linkId%22%3A%229fvFZg3vLGh-QXw8A%22%7D)
3. Keeps Zion, Account Success, and ENav on the same page with group progress
4. ENav team builds the custom portal within 1-2 business days max
5. Build for a Zion only group may take as little as 30 minutes with all necessary information provided and leaving the client to add employees/upload census once they are in the portal
6. Additional team members could be trained to complete build as preferred/needed and/or ENav team could have individual(s) specifically assigned to Zion builds to ensure immediate prioritization

# Benefit Manager emails contract and sends a meeting link

1. See email example below
2. This could again potentially be expedited by the Salesperson sending the BSA for digital signature while on the phone with the client or immediately after the call
3. We have also expedite by having standardized assignment procedures allowing the Salesperson to know in advance who a group would go to. This allows the salesperson to simply cc in the expected Benefit Manager on the initial follow-up email or even go ahead and book a time on the Benefit Manager’s calendar while they still have the client on the phone
4. \*\*standardized assignment structure may need to change and adjust over time given changing needs of the Account Success team but would be monitored and keep Sales team up to date with any changes needed for future group onboarding

Subject: Welcome to Zion Benefits — Next Steps for Your Group

Hi \[Client Name], My name is Canen Hastings and I’ll be your dedicated Benefit Manager as you begin the onboarding process with Zion. I’m looking forward to working with you and helping ensure everything is set up smoothly for your team. What to Expect Next

* You should receive your group contract via Adobe shortly for electronic signature. If you have any questions as you review it, please don’t hesitate to reach out—I’m happy to walk through anything with you.
* Once the contract is signed, the next step is to schedule a meeting with me so we can review your new benefit enrollment platform together. During this session, we’ll:
* Walk through your employer portal
* Confirm your group setup is complete and accurate
* Add your employees
* Kick off enrollment by sending invitations to your team

You can schedule a time that works best for you using my booking link below: [Book Time With Me](https://outlook.office.com/bookwithme/user/e28ab843ab2443f18b190b7a4d498eae%40planstin.com?anonymous\&ismsaljsauthenabled=true)

If you have any questions in the meantime—about the contract, timeline, or onboarding process—I’m here to help.

Looking forward to partnering with you!

Best regards,

\[Benefit Manger]

# Client signs contract and schedules meeting

1. We ideally avoid building groups or getting too far ahead without the contract signed locking the group in

# In meeting Benefit Manager shows

1. How to use the portal
2. Ensures plan selection and contributions are finalized and accurate
3. Helps to upload census or add employees
4. Finalizes timeline for initial enrollment
5. Approves communication to go to employees
6. Reviews all education needs for group
7. Ensures client satisfaction and optimization of the group enrollments

# Enrollment invitations are sent out

1. See example email below
2. This is fully customizable for the group
3. We encourage the client notifies employees directly as well so they know what to expect
4. \*If a client does not want to use SSNs this registration email would also include clarification that in place of SSN they will input the last 4 digits of their phone number (i.e. 001-01-5692)

Subject: New Benefit Offering -Zion HealthShare

Hello Jane,

We’re excited to share that a new benefit option, Zion HealthShare, is now available to Zion Only Demo Company employees.

Zion HealthShare offers an alternative healthcare option focused on community-based sharing of medical expenses. If you’re interested in learning more or enrolling, you’ll need to register your account.

How to Get Started

1. Visit the registration link: [Registration](https://www.employeenavigator.com/benefits/Account/Register)
2. Create your account using our Company Identifier: ZODC
3. \*In place of inserting the last 4 digits of your SSN use the last 4 digits of your phone number

Once registered, you’ll be able to review plan details and cost, complete your enrollment, and return anytime to review information.

If you have questions about eligibility or the enrollment process, please reach out to our Benefit Specialist, Jen Andrade at 435-216-1086 or <jenandrade@planstin.com> .

Benefits will be effective the first of the month after you elect the plans. You'll receive an email at that time with further instructions to access and utilize your benefits.

We’re happy to offer this benefit option and encourage you to explore whether it’s a good fit for you and your family.

Thank you,

Zion Only Demo Company

# Employees register their accounts and enroll

1. Employees register following the instructions above
2. This is the only time they would have to input something in place of an SSN if the group doesn’t want to use those, otherwise we’d already have a number filled in for them
3. Employees continually and automatically receive reminders to enroll during the initial enrollment process and as new hires come onboard to optimize elections
4. Platform is available for employees all year round to review all information link to critical Zion videos and websites
5. Changes can be made throughout the year

# Benefit Specialists guide employees through their choices

1. According to group desires/needs as established between the client and Benefit Manager, Benefit Specialists also reach out to guide employees through step-by-step and ensure that employees understand what they are getting and how to use it to pre-emptively prevent dissatisfaction and optimize enrollment in base plans and add-ons

2. Specialists stay with the group all year round to educate any new employees and provide the same step by step support

3. Custom recorded presentations can be made by the specialist to advertise and explain the plans the group is offering so employees have a custom on-demand resource

4. Specialists actively reach out during enrollment, for new hires, and can be scheduled or called directly for assistance at any time on understanding the plans and making enrollment decisions.

5. We encourage members to speak with a specialist when they are pregnant or expecting to ensure they are getting everything taken care of in advance of the birth

6. Benefit Manager guides client through process

7. The Benefit Manager keeps the client updated on process and ensures all employees are given ample opportunity to enroll and decisions are documented.

8. They guide the client through how to find any necessary payroll deductions

9. Works to optimize account with payroll integration, other benefits all in one system, etc. to make the client “sticky”

10. Addresses any billing questions or concerns

11. Guides the client through their total Benefit Offering Strategy

12. Works with any escalated needs

13. Reviews usage and prepares the group well in advance for annual renewal ensuring all needs continue to be met and the client is retained long-term
